# Commits that reformatted markup without changing what a card says.
#
# tools/stamp_freshness.py passes this file to `git blame`, so a topic touched
# only by a commit listed here keeps the review date it earned rather than the
# date of the reformat. The script infers most such commits itself — see
# global_markup_passes() — and this file is for the ones it cannot.
#
# What it cannot fix: a line that a listed commit *created*. `--ignore-rev`
# reattributes a line to whatever touched it before; a line with no "before"
# stays put. That is why splitting a domain still leaves a few cards dated by
# the split — git's copy detection catches the long runs and misses the short
# ones, and there is nothing earlier in that file to fall back to.
#
# Configure your own blame the same way with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs

